lass=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are about 20 new kiths in the Players Guide, for note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now thats what im talking about!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:44:34-08:00","id":1270158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270125#post1270125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are about 20 new kiths in the Players Guide, for note.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ....the money it keeps bouncing off screen!(...could see one in the next preview?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T22:14:20-08:00","id":1270283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270158#post1270158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> ....the money it keeps bouncing off screen!(...could see one in the next preview?)</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly wouldn\u2019t mind seeing one of them. I\u2019m especially intrigued to see if gremlins are one of them, since they\u2019re mentioned in the preview and I don\u2019t recall seeing them anywhere in C20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T06:16:53-08:00","id":1270335,"title":"","content":"Even as adverse as I've always been to Changeling's almost excessive number of Kiths, this does sound like an interesting setting expansion. I'm curious to see more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T06:31:42-08:00","id":1270344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270335#post1270335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even as adverse as I've always been to Changeling's almost excessive number of Kiths, this does sound like an interesting setting expansion. I'm curious to see more.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is understandable, but with Eurocentric kiths being most of the currently playable options, we looked at adding more kiths as a way to correct that mistake. I wish we\u2019d had more words to do more areas of the world, but we packed a lot into what we did have. There are 4-5 new kiths for each of South America, Africa, the Middle East and Australia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T07:28:39-08:00","id":1270352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270344#post1270344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is understandable, but with Eurocentric kiths being most of the currently playable options, we looked at adding more kiths as a way to correct that mistake. I wish we\u2019d had more words to do more areas of the world, but we packed a lot into what we did have. There are 4-5 new kiths for each of South America, Africa, the Middle East and Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's cool. <br /> <br /> At some point, I started treating the original nine Kiths as broad archetypes rather than specific cultural races, with the &quot;baseline&quot; Kiths being the names and abilities that were common parlance in North America, That way, I could use minor variations as Native American, Japanese and other fae. Redcaps make a good starting point for Pishtacos, for instance (as well as Wendigo and Kappa, among other things). But this is mostly just because of my desire for simplicity. I've always been a sucker for a fun splat. (I really like the Gillhe Dhu, for instance.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T08:26:45-08:00","id":1270359,"title":"","content":"I like the approach that the same kith can have different names. What is the legend of a redcap if not a cannibalistic boogeyperson that paints themselves with the blood of their victims? A wide variety of cultures have that. Big strong guardians? Yep, those too. Animal themed trickster? Everywhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T14:53:19-08:00","id":1270439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270352#post1270352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's cool.<br /> <br /> At some point, I started treating the original nine Kiths as broad archetypes rather than specific cultural races, with the &quot;baseline&quot; Kiths being the names and abilities that were common parlance in North America, That way, I could use minor variations as Native American, Japanese and other fae. Redcaps make a good starting point for Pishtacos, for instance (as well as Wendigo and Kappa, among other things). But this is mostly just because of my desire for simplicity. I've always been a sucker for a fun splat. (I really like the Gillhe Dhu, for instance.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I kind of feel on the other hand there should be greater variety within Kiths proper.. like how there's oba and River Hags.. there should be Pooka with slightly different Brs and frailties(like every trickster may not have issues with truth but might be easily slighted... some animals aren't as trustworthy as others etc) I mean Sidhe get this.. with Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-24T21:55:55-08:00","id":1270525,"title":"","content":"That is sort of what I try to do, say with my Wendigo changelings being a type of Redcap (thou Wendigo would say that Redcaps are a variation of them), with some slight mechanical changes. But sometimes you do need something new. Japanese Snow Women, for example. This is why I'm glad C20 seems to be trying to make it easier for people to design their own Kiths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T08:49:46-08:00","id":1270610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1270525#post1270525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is sort of what I try to do, say with my Wendigo changelings being a type of Redcap (thou Wendigo would say that Redcaps are a variation of them), with some slight mechanical changes. But sometimes you do need something new. Japanese Snow Women, for example. This is why I'm glad C20 seems to be trying to make it easier for people to design their own Kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right I mean I kind of wish the standard were &quot;Pooka&quot; Br-shapeshifting then (Take one of these) and frailty take 1 of these<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I don't feel Oni make good Trolls, but if there were a more generic &quot;Strong guy&quot; kith that both came under like if you had Strength but a frailty &quot;get angry easier&quot; or something like that I would totally combine the two as related.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly I'd hang Yuki-Onna off of some sort of &quot;Succubus&quot; type (I know they try to make a house for this) but a generic social cortesean type rather than Ruler. I think that's kind of a missing base kith idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T01:38:21-08:00","id":1272142,"title":"","content":"I mean Trolls don\u2019t even make good Trolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve seen the each splat is general thing already. I find it rather refreshing and intriguing to have Changeling have each splat niche and what not. So instead I just make say Wendigo a new kith rather then a redcap, well They are Thallain in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T21:22:59-08:00","id":1272300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1272142#post1272142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean Trolls don\u2019t even make good Trolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pooka do make best Trolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> But seriously Troll is pretty much the same as fairy in a many places so its kind of hard for them to live up to everything said about them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T21:32:29-08:00","id":1272301,"title":"","content":"Exactly. The problem is the first Batch of Jiths released for the Game were essentially creations of the game, not really worrying about reflecting myths too much and some like Sluagh and Boggins represent a broad and varied Archetype but took a specific approach to it. But then each later Kith made each Kith a very specific Creature and they much more closely seemed tied to their inspirational myths. So you have Trolls who are Viking Knights who don\u2019t really come from Legends but then we get Selkies who are pretty much taken right from legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T22:14:20-08:00","id":1272305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1272301#post1272301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. The problem is the first Batch of Jiths released for the Game were essentially creations of the game, not really worrying about reflecting myths too much and some like Sluagh and Boggins represent a broad and varied Archetype but took a specific approach to it. But then each later Kith made each Kith a very specific Creature and they much more closely seemed tied to their inspirational myths. So you have Trolls who are Viking Knights who don\u2019t really come from Legends but then we get Selkies who are pretty much taken right from legend.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah big giant knights DO come from legend though. The only real odd kith out in the base is Satyrs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T17:56:15-08:00","id":1272498,"title":"","content":"I think the Trolls were inspired mainly by Norse Jotunn, including ones like Skadi and Gerdr, as well as Welsh giant myths, with bits of the Greek giants thrown in. At least that was the impression I got from the Kith book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T13:27:36-08:00","id":1272684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1272498#post1272498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Trolls were inspired mainly by Norse Jotunn, including ones like Skadi and Gerdr, as well as Welsh giant myths, with bits of the Greek giants thrown in. At least that was the impression I got from the Kith book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they are more like the Jotunn or Ettin kith, but they made em blue and popped on some horns.<br /> <br /> Now Redcaps and Sluagh are more the trolls of myths, what with Underbridge being theirs and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T14:45:11-08:00","id":1272703,"title":"","content":"I always suspected the blue skin was an homage to Robert E. Howard's &quot;The Frost Giant's Daughter&quot;. <br /> <br /> Just personally, I also like to throw in influences from the Basque jentilak (a tendency toward being hirsute and building stuff out of large stones), the Hebrew Anakim, certain Native American legends (the Choctaw and Cherokee have some interesting ones), and 19th century folklore of Paul Bunyan and John Henry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T19:35:03-08:00","id":1272754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1272684#post1272684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they are more like the Jotunn or Ettin kith, but they made em blue and popped on some horns.<br /> <br /> Now Redcaps and Sluagh are more the trolls of myths, what with Underbridge being theirs and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really. Troll is a pretty generic &quot;Faery&quot; name. Sometimes its monsters living under bridges sometimes its giant honorable guys who built some wierd geographic feature, sometimes its small naked people with wierd hair and gems on their belly buttons. Its Like Sidhe or Elves..<br /> <br /> Sluagh are pretty consistantly what they are in both a generic &quot;things that go in the dark&quot; and match up to the myth that gave them their name(which are things in that go bump in the dark)<br /> <br /> Redcaps are.. complicated. It seems Red cap was particular Scotish folklore character, like Baba Yaga in Eastern Europe. Now he was under the broadly under the concept of &quot;Scary murderous goblin thing that eats you&quot;(Though sometime he was more benign like Baba Yaga)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T22:47:48-08:00","id":1272785,"title":"","content":"Elves is generic but it can also be narrowed down in essence to what Sidhe and it translates well to other beings that are similar, like Sidhe and Alfar, and Tolkien elf, but Santa Elves are more Boggan and Knocker.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to see a source that says there is only one creature called the Redcap and all others are confusing the matter. Because from my understanding a few things were treated as a singular creature that died it\u2019s head in blood, but also it has been treated in poems and tales as a group. I think it\u2019s like the Shellycoat, it can be treated as a boogeyman that makes a coat of Shells but it can also be understood as a group of goblins that do so. There are multiple stories of blood as dye goblins, thy even give you some in the nickname category, like Dunthers.<br /> <br /> So while Trolls is a broad term like say elf, it also can refer to specific beings. For instance you don\u2019t call Dragons trolls or werewolves trolls, but you could call tiny men who turn into stone trolls and also call giants who turn into hills trolls. The Prose Edda even has one instance were they mention Troll, as Thor was Smashing Trolls in the East while the Aesir entertained a giant guest.<br /> <br /> But you are missing the point I\u2019m making. The first batch of Kiths were very specific beings, that didn\u2019t need to be that specific as Archtypically they could have fit a wider group of beings. While latter Kiths were very specific beings they fit very specific roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T00:23:33-08:00","id":1272793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1272785#post1272785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elves is generic but it can also be narrowed down in essence to what Sidhe and it translates well to other beings that are similar, like Sidhe and Alfar, and Tolkien elf, but Santa Elves are more Boggan and Knocker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knockers are why Santa never gets you what you really want for Christmas!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019d like to see a source that says there is only one creature called the Redcap and all others are confusing the matter. Because from my understanding a few things were treated as a singular creature that died it\u2019s head in blood, but also it has been treated in poems and tales as a group. I think it\u2019s like the Shellycoat, it can be treated as a boogeyman that makes a coat of Shells but it can also be understood as a group of goblins that do so. There are multiple stories of blood as dye goblins, thy even give you some in the nickname category, like Dunthers. </div> </div> </div>Well I said it was complicated. It seems at one time it was a Singular entity haunting one castle.. then he was haunting multiple castles so it sort of got expanded out into a group, and that guy promoted to Robin Redcap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So while Trolls is a broad term like say elf, it also can refer to specific beings. For instance you don\u2019t call Dragons trolls or werewolves trolls, but you could call tiny men who turn into stone trolls and also call giants who turn into hills trolls. The Prose Edda even has one instance were they mention Troll, as Thor was Smashing Trolls in the East while the Aesir entertained a giant guest. </div> </div> </div>I know its wikipedia.. but... according to that Werewolf is a legitimate translation for the word Troll...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you are missing the point I\u2019m making. The first batch of Kiths were very specific beings, that didn\u2019t need to be that specific as Archtypically they could have fit a wider group of beings. While latter Kiths were very specific beings they fit very specific roles. </div> </div> </div>I would say its a mix? There's alot of myths that reoccur through out the world. Deciding say most House Fairies fall under Boggans isn't really a big stretch.<br /> <br /> Sidhe-debately meant to be all noble elf types but really only expanded into that with the book of Lost houses and were treated as functionally British Imperialists in multiple books(see KB Eshu)<br /> <br /> Sluagh-archtypal CReatures that go bump in the night/faerie things that are connected to dead people.. named after a Scottish thing that very nicely falls under that. I don't think there would be a better way to make a Sluagh kith.<br /> <br /> Pooka-The most broad archetypal Kith I mean is there a culture where &quot;shapeshifting trickster&quot; isn't a thing? <br /> <br /> Boggan-Real myth seems to work for this, but its also a commonly reoccuring myth so..<br /> <br /> Nocker-the Real myth seems to solidly work with this, but could just as easily been Kobald or Goblin.<br /> <br /> Troll-We already went over.<br /> <br /> Satyr-extremely specific basis and myth as much so as any of the add on ones.<br /> <br /> Redcaps are a very specific subset of a very particular myth, it seems like a pretty good fit.<br /> <br /> Eshu-have sort of the problem of not knowing if they want to be a broad archtype or a particular racial connection and it shows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the ones added in previous editions that weren't some form Gallain:<br /> <br /> <br /> We have the Clurichain this actually probably could be expanded out into a variety of similar kiths and... would probably have come off as less of a racist joke.<br /> <br /> The Selkie-could have been expanded into a generic secondary shapeshifter kith(plenty of &quot;i put on my magic thing and transform into...&quot; stories in myth)<br /> <br /> Pixies-generic thief kith in.. all portrayals though named after one of those.<br /> <br /> Green people-not even going to try to write their proper name.. they are a really weird concept all around and I think based entirely on the Green Knight which I'm not sure was a part of a race so much as a wierd thing he did.<br /> <br /> <br /> so honestly I'd say it went back and forth and some kiths they didn't know if they were supposed to be archtypes or particular cultures depending on who was writing them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T07:44:15-08:00","id":1282638,"title":"","content":"The text of the C20 referring to Bellatierra mentions the Kingdom of Amazonia and the Mountain Kingdoms. In the excerpt that was released in internet there is a lot of history about the region, something about the Kingfom of Mountain and the 10 guardians, being one of each kingdom, so I was wondering, will we have short descriptions of the kingdoms, as we had in C20? Texts like Cymru, Iberia, Neutria? As a Brazilian who is eager to have this material in hand to be able to set up local games I would like to know from you, writers who are working on the project, if you could give us more information about what else we can expect from South America in the book, besides the 4 or 5 new regional kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25014-wilkerj","name":"wilkerj","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T09:05:50-08:00","id":1287555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wilkerj</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1282638#post1282638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text of the C20 referring to Bellatierra mentions the Kingdom of Amazonia and the Mountain Kingdoms. In the excerpt that was released in internet there is a lot of history about the region, something about the Kingfom of Mountain and the 10 guardians, being one of each kingdom, so I was wondering, will we have short descriptions of the kingdoms, as we had in C20? Texts like Cymru, Iberia, Neutria? As a Brazilian who is eager to have this material in hand to be able to set up local games I would like to know from you, writers who are working on the project, if you could give us more information about what else we can expect from South America in the book, besides the 4 or 5 new regional kiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies for not seeing this: I'm not on the forums frequently in the last few months due to real life constraints. <br /> <br /> South America, the Middle East, Africa and Australia were expanded as best we could within the word count with their own Dreaming topographies, Dreaming history, and legends and creation myths, as well as their own kiths and kingdoms. Fully one third of the Players' Guide was devoted to showcasing the areas outside of Concordia. Each Kingdom within Bellatierra, if I recall correctly (without the files directly at hand currently), has its own short description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T12:19:03-08:00","id":1287623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1287555#post1287555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My apologies for not seeing this: I'm not on the forums frequently in the last few months due to real life constraints.<br /> <br /> South America, the Middle East, Africa and Australia were expanded as best we could within the word count with their own Dreaming topographies, Dreaming history, and legends and creation myths, as well as their own kiths and kingdoms. Fully one third of the Players' Guide was devoted to showcasing the areas outside of Concordia. Each Kingdom within Bellatierra, if I recall correctly (without the files directly at hand currently), has its own short description.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess that means no India...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-18T08:42:34-08:00","id":1289195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1269836-c20-player-s-guide-bellatierra-preview?p=1287555#post1287555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My apologies for not seeing this: I'm not on the forums frequently in the last few months due to real life constraints.<br /> <br /> South America, the Middle East, Africa and Australia were expanded as best we could within the word count with their own Dreaming topographies, Dreaming history, and legends and creation myths, as well as their own kiths and kingdoms. Fully one third of the Players' Guide was devoted to showcasing the areas outside of Concordia. Each Kingdom within Bellatierra, if I recall correctly (without the files directly at hand currently), has its own short description.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for your response Luka.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to the book's release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25014-wilkerj","name":"wilkerj","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}